# Creating and deleting relations: box-select the Approach Road and Exit Road
# ways (and their nodes), make a relation from them with New Relation in the
# right-click menu, see it selected with its Members list, delete it
# (Backspace), and undo.
#
# Coordinates (window 1200x800, default 280px side panel, viewport as in
# relation-editor.osmscript, same fixture): Approach Road runs from (300,400)
# to (450,400) and Exit Road from (450,400) down to (450,500), so the box
# below encloses both. The context menu opens with its top-left corner at the
# click (340,400); its New Relation row, below Add to Relation…, is centred
# at y=586 (menu entries depend on the selection, so adjust if it changes).

window 1200 800
load_osm docs/screenshots/fixtures/relation-editor.osm
viewport 40.7120 -74.0060 18
wait_idle 5s

drag 270,370 480,530 button=left
wait_idle 2s
capture out/relation-create-delete-01-selected.png

# The context menu lists New Relation.
click 340,400 button=right
wait_idle 2s
capture out/relation-create-delete-02-context-menu.png

# Clicking it makes the relation and selects it: Tags and Members show in the
# panel.
click 400,586
wait_idle 2s
capture out/relation-create-delete-03-created.png

# Delete removes the relation but not its members.
key backspace
wait_idle 2s
capture out/relation-create-delete-04-deleted.png

# Undo brings it back, with its members.
key cmd+z
wait_idle 2s
capture out/relation-create-delete-05-delete-undone.png
log done
